    "created_at": "2018-08-27T07:25:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-27T07:25:44Z",
    "body": "That would probably work, but then you can't use \"fire an event\" for those events. And if we wanted to enable that, which would make sense, we'd have to redefine how the IDL attributes are initialized and refactor all callers.\r\n\r\n(Multiple optional arguments also gets a little ugly and might warrant some refactoring of the callers.)",
